=== SURVEY ===
Cited code paths verified to exist and to match the bug description:

1. internal/signal/live_store.go:215-218
   `HybridLiveSignalStore.GetAll` returns `freshSignalValues(values, s.now())` when L2
   returns a non-empty map. The L1 fallback at lines 215-216 (`if len(values) == 0`)
   only triggers when the raw Redis hash is empty, NOT when the freshness filter
   strips everything. This matches failure (1) and (2) in the prompt.

2. internal/signal/live_store.go:256-280 (`hydrateMissingValues`)
   Used by `Warm`. Skips entries with `value.Timestamp.IsZero()` (legacy scalar
   Redis values). Confirms that legacy scalars never enter L1 even after Warm,
   so they are silently dropped on every read path that goes through L2 first.

3. internal/service/vehicle_service.go contains `BuildStateFromSignalStore`
   (file confirmed via grep). Per the prompt, only `state.State` has a DB
   fallback; numeric/string fields fall to zero when the live map is empty.

4. internal/database/signal_log_reader_query.go:28-33
   `SignalLogReader.SnapshotAt(ctx, vehicleID, at)` already exists and returns
   the latest value of every signal for a vehicle at or before `at`. This is
   the durable L3 read that ADR-001 promises and is the correct source for the
   missing fallback in `BuildStateFromSignalStore`.

5. .github/ARCHITECTURE.md:9 (ADR-001 Unified Signal Log) and
   .github/ARCHITECTURE.md:37 (ADR-007 Live Signal State Layering) both exist
   and define the L1/L2/L3 contract referenced in this decision record.

No additional files were inspected. No source files were modified. No production
systems were inspected.

=== REASONING ===
Phase 38 is bug-fix-only. It addresses a user-visible regression where the
dashboard endpoint `GET /api/v1/vehicles/{id}/state` reports zeros for fields
(odometer, inside_temp, outside_temp, software_version, ...) whose values are
present in Redis (`vehicle:{id}:signals` HSET) and signal_log.

Three independent failures, each verified above, combine into the symptom:

  (a) `HybridLiveSignalStore.GetAll` strips legacy scalar entries
      (Timestamp.IsZero()) and >2-minute-stale entries via `freshSignalValues`,
      and only consults L1 when the *raw* Redis hash is empty. After the filter
      empties the result, callers see "no live data" and zero out the response.

  (b) `Warm` / `hydrateMissingValues` refuses to promote legacy scalars into
      L1, so the L1 path can never compensate for (a) on existing fleets that
      have legacy Redis values.

  (c) `service.VehicleService.BuildStateFromSignalStore` has DB fallback only
      for `state.State`. There is no signal_log "last known value" lookup for
      numeric/string fields, even though `SignalLogReader.SnapshotAt` already
      exposes that read. ADR-001 designates signal_log as the durable source
      of truth; this fallback is the existing-but-unused L3 read it promises.

Approved scope of Phase 38 (bug-fix-only):

  Change 1: Stop dropping stale and legacy values from `GetAll` in a way that
            silently zeroes the dashboard. Either return the unfiltered map and
            let callers decide freshness, or fall through to L1 when the
            filtered map is empty. No new Redis keys, no new schema.

  Change 2: Add a signal_log fallback for missing fields in
            `BuildStateFromSignalStore` using `SignalLogReader.SnapshotAt`.
            This uses the L3 read ADR-001 already designates as durable
            history; it does NOT introduce snapshot-table reads (positions,
            security_events, climate_snapshots, etc.) that ADR-001/ADR-007
            forbid.

  Change 3: Restamp legacy `Timestamp.IsZero()` Redis entries during `Warm`
            (or on first observation) so the L1/L2 contract converges to
            ADR-007's "live values older than 2 minutes are stale; legacy
            scalars are unknown freshness". Restamping uses the current write
            time only when promoting into L1 from a legacy scalar and is
            scoped so it does not falsify true freshness.

ADR alignment:

  ADR-001 (Unified Signal Log): Preserved. signal_log remains the single
          source of truth for durable history. Change 2 USES SnapshotAt; it
          does not add a new write path or new snapshot tables.

  ADR-007 (Live Signal State Layering): Preserved. L1 SignalStore stays the
          local hot-path store for telemetry/FSM/sessions. L2 RedisSignalCache
          stays the cross-pod current-state cache and SSE fanout. L3 signal_log
          stays the durable history. The keys
          `vehicle:{vehicleID}:signals`, `vehicle_signals`, and
          `signal_log:backlog` are unchanged. The 2-minute live-staleness rule
          is unchanged.

What Phase 38 will NOT do (explicit non-goals, to defend the contract):

  - No new schema migrations.
  - No new API surface or new endpoints.
  - No reads from snapshot tables (positions, climate_snapshots,
    security_events, motor_snapshots, tire_pressure_snapshots,
    media_snapshots, safety_snapshots) for "current value" answers.
  - No removal of the SignalStore L1 hot path.
  - No making Redis a synchronous blocker for MQTT/telemetry ingestion.
  - No claim of active-active FSM/reconciliation across pods without
    vehicle-owner routing or leases.
  - No widening of LIVE_SIGNAL_STORE_MODE semantics (`local` remains the
    rollback switch).

Decision: Approve all three changes as bug-fix scope. Subsequent prompts in
Phase 38 will implement, test, and gate each change individually.

